<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karachi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karachi is the largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> province, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> coast near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> delta. A small trading town in the 18th century, it grew under British rule from 1843 into a major port. It was the first capital of Pakistan from 1947 until the government moved north in 1959, and it remains the country's main commercial and financial centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karachi.jpg" alt="Karachi" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ktownboy103 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clifton_Karachi_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
